            <ArticleTitle>Double-blind study of the analgesic effect of indoprofen (K 4277).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a double-blind study, indoprofen was superior to placebo in decreasing pain in patients with primary and metastatic cancer and with neuralgia. A single oral dose of 200 mg was more active than a 100-mg dose. The preferences of patients proved to be a more sensitive parameter in this study than scores of pain intensity, pain relief, and other related measurements (SPID, TOTPAR, and Peak PID).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
